|~ The binding the command line adds to the root of the tree of names:
   its provider, `::cli`, whose module `cli.qlang` declares its verbs
   and their refusals. ~|

:cli
  |~~ The command line of qlang: `@in`, `@out`, `@err` and `@tap` read
      and write the streams of the process, and `table` renders a
      vector of maps as text. A value one query hands another over a
      pipe keeps its kinds as its literal: `print | @out` writes it and
      `@in | parse | open` reads it back.
      A query runs on what stdin holds: JSON read as values, an object
      a map whose keys are keywords, whose answer is written as JSON,
      where a value JSON has no form for is refused; text read
      as a string, whose answer is written as its `print`; and
      `| json` writes JSON text. A query that writes to stdout itself,
      by `@out`, holds the channel, and its answer is left unwritten.
      Every query the command line runs calls its verbs by their names,
      and `::cli | manifest` lists them.
  ~~|
